<item>
            <title>[LU-20932] lnet: route round robin is not wrap-safe, and router_sensitivity docs are stale</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20932</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Problem&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The route round robin in &lt;tt&gt;lnet_find_route_locked()&lt;/tt&gt; is not wrap-safe. After 2^31 routed sends to one remote net, &lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; wraps. From then on, one route takes all the traffic to that net, and the round robin does not recover.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18444&quot; title=&quot;LNet health router sensitivity may lead to no routes alive&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18444&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18444&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;router_sensitivity_percentage&lt;/tt&gt; has no effect. Three comments and the &lt;tt&gt;lnetctl&lt;/tt&gt; help text still describe the old effect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Environment&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Environment&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master at 4a7bddaf15. The &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18444&quot; title=&quot;LNet health router sensitivity may lead to no routes alive&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18444&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18444&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fix (70c5f58403) is in this tree.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Any node that sends to one remote net through 2 or more routes with equal priority, hops and gateway health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Reproduction&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproduction&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Configure 2 routes to one remote net with equal priority and hops.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Send 2^31 or more messages through the 2 routes. To get there faster, use a debugger to set &lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; of both routes near &lt;tt&gt;INT_MAX&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Look at the gateway of each send in the D_NET log (&quot;Selected next-hop&quot;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Result: all sends use one route.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Analysis&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Analysis&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;struct lnet_route&lt;/tt&gt; is an &lt;tt&gt;int&lt;/tt&gt;. After each routed send, &lt;tt&gt;lnet_handle_find_routed_path()&lt;/tt&gt; sets &lt;tt&gt;best_route-&amp;gt;lr_seq = last_route-&amp;gt;lr_seq + 1&lt;/tt&gt;. Thus the largest &lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; on the net grows by 1 for each send.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lnet_find_route_locked()&lt;/tt&gt; picks two routes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;last_route&lt;/tt&gt; is the route with the largest &lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;last_route-&amp;gt;lr_seq &amp;lt; route-&amp;gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;best_route&lt;/tt&gt; is the route with the smallest &lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; among equal routes (&lt;tt&gt;route-&amp;gt;lr_seq &amp;gt; best_route-&amp;gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; skips a route).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Example with routes A and B. A has &lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; &lt;tt&gt;INT_MAX&lt;/tt&gt;. The next send uses B and sets B to &lt;tt&gt;INT_MAX + 1&lt;/tt&gt;, which wraps to &lt;tt&gt;INT_MIN&lt;/tt&gt;. Now B has the smallest value, and A has the largest. Each send then picks B and sets B to &lt;tt&gt;INT_MAX + 1&lt;/tt&gt; again. A gets no more traffic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18444&quot; title=&quot;LNet health router sensitivity may lead to no routes alive&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18444&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18444&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, the &lt;tt&gt;last_route&lt;/tt&gt; compare used a difference (&lt;tt&gt;last_route-&amp;gt;lr_seq - route-&amp;gt;lr_seq &amp;lt; 0&lt;/tt&gt;). With that compare, the skew stopped after about 2^32 sends. The &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18444&quot; title=&quot;LNet health router sensitivity may lead to no routes alive&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18444&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18444&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; refactor changed it to a plain compare, so the skew is now permanent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The stale text:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lnet/lnet/router.c&lt;/tt&gt;: the comment above &lt;tt&gt;router_sensitivity_percentage&lt;/tt&gt; describes the old health threshold.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lnet/utils/lnetctl.c&lt;/tt&gt;: the &lt;tt&gt;lnetctl set router_sensitivity&lt;/tt&gt; help says that 100 needs fully healthy router interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lnet/utils/lnetconfig/liblnetconfig.h&lt;/tt&gt;: the &lt;tt&gt;lustre_lnet_config_rtr_sensitivity&lt;/tt&gt; comment says that LNet treats an interface below the percentage as failed.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lnet/lnet/lib-msg.c&lt;/tt&gt;: a comment says that routers &quot;rely on health feature to manage route and peer aliveness&quot;. Route aliveness now uses only the NI status. Peer NI health only ranks gateways and MR forwarding paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Proposedfix&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Make &lt;tt&gt;lr_seq&lt;/tt&gt; an &lt;tt&gt;unsigned int&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Compare with a signed difference, as &lt;tt&gt;time_after()&lt;/tt&gt; does: &lt;tt&gt;(int)(route-&amp;gt;lr_seq - last_route-&amp;gt;lr_seq) &amp;gt; 0&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;(int)(route-&amp;gt;lr_seq - best_route-&amp;gt;lr_seq) &amp;gt; 0&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In the &lt;tt&gt;router.c&lt;/tt&gt; comment, the &lt;tt&gt;lnetctl&lt;/tt&gt; help and &lt;tt&gt;liblnetconfig.h&lt;/tt&gt;, say that &lt;tt&gt;router_sensitivity_percentage&lt;/tt&gt; is deprecated and has no effect.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Change the &lt;tt&gt;lib-msg.c&lt;/tt&gt; comment: gateway selection and MR forwarding use peer NI health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The finding is source-only. We did not run the wrap on a VM.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
